\subsection{Environment and Training Details}
\label{sec:env_details}

All experiments use Walker Walk and Cheetah Run from the DeepMind Control Suite (DMC; \citealt{tassa2018dmcontrol}) with proprioceptive observations, chosen for their contrasting dynamics (6-joint biped vs.\ 2-joint runner). Walker Walk serves as the primary environment with the full factorial design; Cheetah Run serves as a severity-dependent generalization probe: CIVO manifests at $8$--$70\times$ NVE on Cheetah versus $2$--$5\times$ on Walker, testing whether interventions transfer under amplified severity rather than replicating the full factorial. The baseline runs for 500K steps (peak return 970.4); treatments run for 105K steps, sufficient to observe collapse onset. All hyperparameters follow the DreamerV3 defaults \citep{hafner2023dreamerv3} without task-specific tuning ($d{=}32$ temporal embedding; full hyperparameters in Appendix~\ref{sec:hyperparameters}). Training uses a single NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 GPU (${\sim}80$ GPU-hours total). The codebase extends the official DreamerV3 implementation\footnote{\url{https://github.com/danijar/dreamerv3}, accessed March 2026.} with the variable-rate modules described in \S\ref{sec:variable_rate}.

\section{Results}
\label{sec:results}

We organize results around seven findings (F1--F7) that establish a causal chain from trained temporal conditioning to pathological value dynamics. All experiments use Walker Walk (DMC) with DreamerV3; treatments run to 105K steps and the baseline to 505K steps. We report evaluation returns (mean over 10 episodes) and the normalized value-to-eval ratio ($\nve$, \S\ref{sec:metrics}).

